# The image needs only what the Dockerfile COPYs: app/, config/, scripts/ and
# requirements.txt. Everything else is dev tooling, secrets, or local state and
# must never enter the build context (it would bloat the image and risk baking
# in a credential or the local database).
#
# Strategy: exclude everything, then re-include exactly what ships.

*

!app
!config
!scripts
!requirements.txt
!requirements-sftp.txt

# Re-exclude junk that could live under the re-included dirs.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.DS_Store
